01:02:27.174 --> 01:02:32.116
In the Age of Grace, Jesus was the name of
God.

01:02:32.141 --> 01:02:38.665
In the Age of Kingdom, His name will be
Almighty God.

01:02:38.690 --> 01:02:42.267
So, speaking of this, right?

01:02:42.291 --> 01:02:45.551
Oh, that's okay, Brother Dracos.

01:02:45.576 --> 01:02:47.179
I had a thought.

01:02:47.204 --> 01:02:49.205
Don't doubt yourself, my dear brother.

01:02:49.230 --> 01:02:50.563
Don't doubt yourself.

01:02:50.588 --> 01:02:54.006
If you feel like you're right,
you put it there, okay, brother?

01:02:54.031 --> 01:02:56.906
It has a nice ring to it, right,
Brother Warren?

01:02:56.930 --> 01:02:57.630
Because He's the...

01:02:57.730 --> 01:03:02.935
He's coming back as the Almighty to
conquer all.

01:03:02.960 --> 01:03:04.725
Yeah, it does have a nice ring to it.

01:03:04.750 --> 01:03:06.028
Amen, everybody.

01:03:06.052 --> 01:03:09.202
So,
perhaps some of you are probably asking,

01:03:09.227 --> 01:03:11.651
well,
why does God need to change His name?

01:03:11.676 --> 01:03:13.997
What is the significance of this?

01:03:14.022 --> 01:03:20.716
Well, we will understand after reading a
few passages of words together.

01:03:20.750 --> 01:03:21.865
All right?

01:03:21.890 --> 01:03:23.900
So, let me send it to the group.

01:03:23.925 --> 01:03:27.883
Let's listen to a few passages of words
together, and let's understand why.

01:03:27.908 --> 01:03:31.185
Why does God have to take on a new name?

01:03:31.210 --> 01:03:32.500
Right?

01:03:32.525 --> 01:03:37.559
I think brothers and sisters may already
know, but let's listen together.

01:03:37.584 --> 01:03:42.871
In each age, God does new work and is
called by a new name. 

01:03:42.895 --> 01:03:47.207
How could He do the same work in different
ages?

01:03:47.232 --> 01:03:50.080
How could He cling to the old?

01:03:50.105 --> 01:03:55.879
The name of Jesus was taken for the sake
of the work of redemption.

01:03:55.904 --> 01:04:02.321
So, would He still be called by the same
name when He returns in the last days?

01:04:02.346 --> 01:04:06.212
Would He still be doing the work of
redemption?

01:04:06.237 --> 01:04:10.841
Why is it
that Jehovah and Jesus are one, yet, 

01:04:10.866 --> 01:04:14.985
they are called
by different names in different ages?

01:04:15.010 --> 01:04:19.211
Is it not because the ages of their work
are different?

01:04:19.236 --> 01:04:24.271
Could a single name represent God in His
entirety?

01:04:24.296 --> 01:04:30.510
This being so, God must be called by a
different name in a different age,

01:04:30.535 --> 01:04:37.046
and He must use the name to change the age
and to represent the age.

01:04:37.071 --> 01:04:41.440
For no one name can fully represent God
Himself.

01:04:41.465 --> 01:04:44.930
And
each name is able only to represent the

01:04:44.955 --> 01:04:48.986
temporal
aspect of God's disposition in a given age.

01:04:49.011 --> 01:04:53.166
All it needs to do is to represent His
work.

01:04:53.191 --> 01:04:56.911
Therefore,
God can choose whatever name befits

01:04:56.912 --> 01:05:01.440
His
disposition to represent the entire age.

01:05:01.465 --> 01:05:03.410
Amen.

01:05:03.435 --> 01:05:09.831
And the second one reads, In every age in
which God personally does His own work,

01:05:09.856 --> 01:05:13.159
He
uses a name that befits the age in order

01:05:13.160 --> 01:05:16.932
to
encapsulate the work that He intends to do.

01:05:16.957 --> 01:05:22.263
He uses this particular name, one that
possesses the significance of that age,

01:05:22.288 --> 01:05:25.273
to represent His disposition in that age.

01:05:25.298 --> 01:05:32.825
This is God using the language of mankind
to express His own disposition.

01:05:32.850 --> 01:05:34.146
Amen.

01:05:34.171 --> 01:05:35.877
Amen, brothers and sisters.

01:05:35.902 --> 01:05:39.610
So, after reading those words,
we can understand the significance of God

01:05:39.611 --> 01:05:45.446
taking on a new name is the fact that God
is always new and never old.

01:05:45.471 --> 01:05:46.443
You know what that means?

01:05:46.468 --> 01:05:48.466
God is always new and never old?

01:05:48.491 --> 01:05:52.491
It means that God's work is always moving
forward.

01:05:52.516 --> 01:05:57.647
God's name changes along with the age and
the work that He is doing.

01:05:57.672 --> 01:06:04.335
So, every time God does a new stage of
work, every time He begins a new age,

01:06:04.360 --> 01:06:12.290
He actually takes a name with specific
significance for that age, to represent

01:06:12.291 --> 01:06:16.161
the work He is doing and the disposition
He is expressing.

01:06:16.186 --> 01:06:23.459
So this way, we will not confine God to
just the name of Jehovah or Jesus.

01:06:23.484 --> 01:06:30.134
And we will not define God based on our
own notions and imaginations.

01:06:30.159 --> 01:06:34.473
Because we all know what God has and is,
is all incompatible.

01:06:34.498 --> 01:06:37.336
You
know God is wise, He is almighty, that no

01:06:37.337 --> 01:06:41.303
human
language simply cannot fully describe Him.

01:06:41.328 --> 01:06:45.600
No single name could ever fully represent
everything God has and is.

01:06:45.625 --> 01:06:49.774
So God takes on different names in
different age.

01:06:49.799 --> 01:06:56.015
So, in the age of law, God's name was
Jehovah, which represented the work 

01:06:56.040 --> 01:07:01.871
God did in that age, in the disposition of
mercy, majesty, and wrath that He expressed.

01:07:01.896 --> 01:07:08.844
And after that, God personally became flesh
and appeared to work as the Son of Man.

01:07:08.869 --> 01:07:12.911
And He used the
name Jesus to do the work of redemption,

01:07:12.912 --> 01:07:18.188
which ended the
age of law and ushered in the age of grace.

01:07:18.213 --> 01:07:21.330
You see, the Lord Jesus showed people the
way of repentance.

01:07:21.355 --> 01:07:22.825
He forgave their sins.

01:07:22.850 --> 01:07:29.208
He gave them abundant grace and was ultimately
crucified to redeem all of humanity.

01:07:29.233 --> 01:07:35.280
The name of Jesus, it represents the work
of redemption that He did in the age of

01:07:35.305 --> 01:07:40.469
grace and the disposition of mercy,
loving kindness that He also expressed.

01:07:40.494 --> 01:07:43.881
But in the last days, brothers and
sisters, when the Lord Jesus comes back

01:07:43.905 --> 01:07:50.319
again, He will do so under the name of
Almighty God.

01:07:50.344 --> 01:07:52.883
And He will usher in the age of kingdom.

01:07:52.907 --> 01:07:54.839
He
will express the truth to carry out the

01:07:54.864 --> 01:07:57.367
work
of judgment beginning at the house of God.

01:07:57.392 --> 01:07:59.364
And
He does this to completely save us from sin

01:07:59.365 --> 01:08:01.967
once and
for all, and to make a group of overcomers.

01:08:01.992 --> 01:08:04.235
And after that, what do you think is going
to happen?

01:08:04.260 --> 01:08:07.796
The great disasters
will run down, brothers and sisters,

01:08:07.797 --> 01:08:11.276
to punish
the wicked, but also to reward His people.

01:08:11.301 --> 01:08:15.799
God wants to destroy this dark,
evil, old, wicked world.

01:08:15.824 --> 01:08:17.188
He does.

01:08:17.213 --> 01:08:23.791
Because that's the only way that the kingdom
of Christ will finally appear on earth.

01:08:23.816 --> 01:08:29.358
So the name Almighty, it represents God's
inherent disposition.

01:08:29.383 --> 01:08:31.197
All that God has and is.

01:08:31.222 --> 01:08:36.726
So in the last days, the incarnate
Almighty God, He just comes to speak.

01:08:36.751 --> 01:08:40.771
Because only with the words will He judge
and expose our corruption.

01:08:40.796 --> 01:08:44.073
Only with the words He will cleanse and
save us.

01:08:44.098 --> 01:08:48.210
Only with the words He also punishes all
enemy forces of sin.

01:08:48.235 --> 01:08:50.560
And He will establish His kingdom.

01:08:50.585 --> 01:08:57.179
And everything is established and
accomplished through the mouth of Christ.

01:08:57.204 --> 01:09:01.221
Which really shows, God's all mightiness.

01:09:01.246 --> 01:09:07.124
So the name Almighty God, is actually the
most suitable for the age of kingdom.

01:09:07.149 --> 01:09:08.040
Right?

01:09:08.065 --> 01:09:09.550
It's very suitable, brothers and sisters.

01:09:09.575 --> 01:09:12.443
And I actually want to give you an
example.

01:09:12.468 --> 01:09:14.215
Let me give you an example here.

01:09:14.240 --> 01:09:15.010
Okay?

01:09:15.035 --> 01:09:21.734
Let's say for example, you, if you are a
teacher at a school.

01:09:21.758 --> 01:09:25.857
How are students going to address you,
brothers and sisters?

01:09:25.882 --> 01:09:28.564
They're going to address you as a teacher.

01:09:28.590 --> 01:09:29.590
Right?

01:09:29.615 --> 01:09:36.059
And if you became a doctor, then you would
be addressed as a doctor.

01:09:36.084 --> 01:09:39.967
But
if you opened up a store and became the

01:09:39.992 --> 01:09:44.810
owner,
then of course, you would be the boss.

01:09:44.834 --> 01:09:53.456
You see brothers and sisters, when your
profession changes, if your title does not

01:09:53.481 --> 01:09:58.550
change, then people are not going to know
your new profession.

01:09:58.575 --> 01:10:04.284
So when your profession changes,
your title needs to change as well.

01:10:04.309 --> 01:10:09.935
Even though
others call you by a different name or by a

01:10:09.960 --> 01:10:14.950
different title,
you are still the same person, aren't you?

01:10:14.975 --> 01:10:18.480
The same principle applies to God.

01:10:18.505 --> 01:10:23.161
In
different era, in different ages,

01:10:23.162 --> 01:10:28.611
God does different work
to open up the new age with a new name.

01:10:28.636 --> 01:10:36.579
So although God's name may change,
and although His work may change,

01:10:36.604 --> 01:10:39.342
brothers and sisters, you have to
understand something.

01:10:39.367 --> 01:10:41.268
Welcome Vicki and Foylene.

01:10:41.293 --> 01:10:43.943
God's essence, that will never change.

01:10:43.968 --> 01:10:51.709
Almighty God, Jesus, Jehovah, it's still
the same God doing God's work.

01:10:51.734 --> 01:10:56.619
In other words, God's essence,
that will never change.

01:10:56.644 --> 01:11:01.145
But yes, God's name, that can change.

01:11:01.170 --> 01:11:02.890
That can change, brothers and sisters.

01:11:02.915 --> 01:11:03.350
Okay?

01:11:03.375 --> 01:11:07.674
Does that make sense so far, brothers and
sisters?

01:11:07.699 --> 01:11:11.195
Are we clear so far?

01:11:11.220 --> 01:11:11.937
Amen.

01:11:11.962 --> 01:11:13.853
What about others?

01:11:13.878 --> 01:11:17.095
Clear so far, right, brothers and sisters?

01:11:17.133 --> 01:11:19.461
Amen.

01:11:19.486 --> 01:11:20.306
Amen.

01:11:20.331 --> 01:11:22.543
Thanks be to God.

01:11:22.568 --> 01:11:26.252
Amen, brothers and sisters.

01:11:26.277 --> 01:11:27.600
Praise be to God.

01:11:27.625 --> 01:11:30.519
Yeah, it'll never change, okay?

01:11:30.544 --> 01:11:34.537
It'll never, ever, ever, ever change,
brothers and sisters.

01:11:34.562 --> 01:11:39.243
Let's, let's listen, let's read two
passages here together.

01:11:39.268 --> 01:11:40.900
I have two passages, okay?

01:11:40.925 --> 01:11:43.172
Would
any brother or sister like to help me read

01:11:43.173 --> 01:11:45.881
the first
one, and then I can read the second one?

01:11:45.906 --> 01:11:50.268
Or I can read the first one, and someone
can read the second one, okay?

01:11:50.293 --> 01:11:53.740
Because I know a lot of people will say,
well, Sister Thelma, doesn't the Bible

01:11:53.741 --> 01:11:57.590
say, the Lord Jesus Christ, the same
yesterday, today, and forever?

01:11:57.615 --> 01:12:00.872
but you see, a lot of people take
Bible verses out of context.

01:12:00.897 --> 01:12:04.384
When the Bible says, Jesus Christ,
the same yesterday, today, and forever,

01:12:04.410 --> 01:12:07.687
that's not referring to his name,
at all.

01:12:07.712 --> 01:12:13.480
Instead, okay, Yanis, I'll read the first
one, and I'll, you can read the second.

01:12:13.505 --> 01:12:18.720
Oh, Andrea, you read the first one,
and Yanis will read the second one, then.

01:12:18.745 --> 01:12:21.823
Yeah,
you go ahead and open up your mic, Sister Andrea,

01:12:21.848 --> 01:12:26.115

since you will read the first one.

01:12:26.140 --> 01:12:28.035
Can you hear me?

01:12:28.060 --> 01:12:33.456
so, brothers and sisters, when the Bible
says, Jesus Christ, the same yesterday,

01:12:33.480 --> 01:12:37.783
today, and forever, it actually only means
God's disposition.

01:12:37.808 --> 01:12:40.054
All right, doesn't mean his name will
never change.

01:12:40.080 --> 01:12:43.820
Go ahead, Sister Andrea, you can read the
first one for us, my dear sis.

01:12:43.845 --> 01:12:48.514
Where it says, there are those who say
that God is forever unchanging.

01:12:48.540 --> 01:12:50.610
You got it.

01:12:50.634 --> 01:12:54.554
Okay, there are those who say that God is
forever unchanging.

01:12:54.580 --> 01:12:56.070
That is correct.

01:12:56.095 --> 01:13:01.100
But it means that God's disposition,
and his essence are unchanging.

01:13:01.125 --> 01:13:07.837
Changes in his name and work do not prove
that his essence has changed.

01:13:07.862 --> 01:13:12.675
In other words, God will always be God,
and this will never change.

01:13:12.700 --> 01:13:18.700
If you say that the work of God is
unchanging, then would it be possible for

01:13:18.701 --> 01:13:22.895
his 6,000 year management plan to come to
an end?

01:13:22.920 --> 01:13:27.025
You only know that God is forever
unchanging.

01:13:27.050 --> 01:13:31.610
But do you know that God is always new and
never old?

01:13:31.635 --> 01:13:34.932
If the
work of God never changed, could he have

01:13:34.933 --> 01:13:38.408
led
mankind all the way to the present day?

01:13:38.433 --> 01:13:44.816
If God were forever unchanging,
why did he already do the work of two ages?

01:13:44.841 --> 01:13:53.793
The words, God is forever unchanging,
refer to what God inherently has and is.

01:13:53.818 --> 01:14:00.651
Regardless, you cannot confine the work of
6,000 years to a single point,

01:14:00.676 --> 01:14:04.784
or circumscribe it with dead words.

01:14:04.809 --> 01:14:07.434
Such is the ignorance of man.

01:14:07.460 --> 01:14:14.424
God is not as simple as man imagines,
and his work cannot linger in any one age.

01:14:14.449 --> 01:14:19.633
Jehovah, for example, cannot always stand
for the name of God.

01:14:19.658 --> 01:14:23.785
God can also do his work under the name of
Jesus.

01:14:23.809 --> 01:14:30.291
This is a sign that God's work is always
progressing in a forward direction.

01:14:30.316 --> 01:14:32.446
Beautiful reading, my dear sister.

01:14:32.470 --> 01:14:35.145
Brother Yannis, would you like to read the
second one?

01:14:35.170 --> 01:14:37.024
Yes.

01:14:37.049 --> 01:14:40.758
God is always God, and he will never
become Satan.

01:14:40.783 --> 01:14:44.005
Satan is always Satan, and he will never
become God.

01:14:44.030 --> 01:14:49.143
God's wisdom, God's wonderness,
God's righteousness, and God's majesty

01:14:49.168 --> 01:14:50.168
shall never change.

01:14:50.193 --> 01:14:55.413
His essence and what he has, and his
faithfulness shall never ever change.

01:14:55.438 --> 01:15:00.412
As for his work, it is progressing in a
forward direction.

01:15:00.437 --> 01:15:01.844
Let's go deeper.

01:15:01.870 --> 01:15:03.825
It is always God's work.

01:15:03.850 --> 01:15:06.616
He is always new, and never always old.

01:15:06.641 --> 01:15:10.067
In every age, God assumes a new name.

01:15:10.092 --> 01:15:12.479
In every age, he does new work.

01:15:12.504 --> 01:15:15.604
And
in every age, he allows us created beings

01:15:15.605 --> 01:15:20.275
to see
his new intentions and new dispositions.

01:15:20.299 --> 01:15:21.312
